            "description": "",
            "summary": "Largo (TSX:LGO) has just secured a deal with five Brazilian banks to defer $84.2 million in debt repayments until 2026. This move unlocks added flexibility for the company's balance sheet over the next year. See our latest analysis for Largo. Largo\u2019s deal to defer its major debt obligations comes at a dramatic moment for its shareholders. The stock has soared in the past month, with a 30-day share price return of 57.1% and a remarkable 90-day gain of 86.2%. Momentum is clearly building after...",
